	(text "USB-powered DevKit; J1 / 5V unused on carrier.\nJ19 supplies +3V3. All three GND sockets connected.\nOnboard USB-UART, regulator, BOOT and EN retained."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 28 157 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "367f7b73-6288-5090-896d-7c81b8097f0b")
	)
	(text "PAIR: A12 / GPIO19 to A13 / GND\nPAUSE/WIN: J13 / GPIO32 to GND (SW3 retired)\nAll released HIGH; pressed LOW.\nNo carrier BOOT or reset circuitry."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 175 130 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "6d9e2789-cf4b-5b85-818d-3aaca8f5e605")
	)
	(text "SCHEMATIC REVIEW / RELEASE HOLDS\n1. U1 uses A1-A19 / J1-J19 from SigilBackMarked.png (BACK view); never exchange row identities.\n2. No DevKit footprint assigned: measure pitch, row spacing, outline, USB-C overhang, holes, socket height and keepouts.\n3. Future footprint: two 1x19 female sockets, unmistakable A1/J1 marks; verify insertion from carrier component side.\n4. Keep USB-C, BOOT and EN/reset accessible; preserve antenna/component clearances after measurement.\n5. Display connector and buzzer circuit are unresolved logical interfaces, excluded from PCB and BOM.\n6. Old GPIO4 auxiliary and GPIO32 display-detect removed; GPIO32 / J13 is now the Pause/Win button (SW5).\n7. Rev A is an electrical draft, NOT fabrication-ready. Power through DevKit USB; no second supply designed."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 28 211 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "95d26e46-55d7-5517-9943-17b42b09c84d")
	)
